course: dictionary
lesson: 9098
title: Sly and the sneaky side of clever
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sly means clever in a sneaky way. A sly person is good at tricking people and hiding what they really plan. «The new boy has a nice personality» sounds like praise, but when a friend says it and means he is not good-looking, the praise is a trick. Look at the words around sly to find the clue.
explain: Sly can also describe a look, a smile, a grin or a wink. A sly look shows that someone knows a secret or a joke that others do not. «Mia gave a sly smile» tells you Mia knows something the others don't, so ask yourself what she might know.
explain: The phrase «on the sly» means secretly, so that others do not notice. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «secretly» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Sly means clever in a sneaky way, good at tricking people and hiding what you really plan.
fact: A sly look, smile, grin or wink shows that someone knows a secret or a joke that others do not.
fact: «On the sly» means secretly, so that others do not notice.
fact: Sly can also be written slyer and slyest, or slier and sliest. The adverb is slyly, and the noun is slyness.
fact: In Zootopia, Nick Wilde is a sly fox trickster, and Judy Hopps is a brave police officer; the two become best friends.
exercise: «A friend says the new boy has a nice personality, but he is not good-looking.» Why might the friend be sly? | Because they want to give the boy a present | Because they say he is very tall | *Because they say something unkind while seeming to praise | Because they are a new friend
exercise: «Mia gave a sly smile, because she knew the surprise party was tomorrow.» What does sly suggest? | She is very sleepy | She is lost | *She knows a secret that others do not | She is cross with everyone
exercise: What does «on the sly» mean? | Happily, with a song | *Secretly, so others do not notice | Very fast | Loudly, in front of everyone
test: In the story, the sly fox tricked the hen. What does sly mean here? | *Clever in a sneaky way | Very loud | Lazy and tired | Kind and gentle
test: What is the adverb form of sly? | *Slyly | Sliest | Slow | Slyness
exam: Which sentence uses sly correctly? | The sly children are eating lunch | The sly sun shone over the hills | *The sly fox waited quietly until the hens went to sleep | The sly bread was baked this morning
